ve strategy to weaponize northern Iraq. By staging a provocative attack and framing Tehran, foreign intelligence operators seek to ignite anti-Iranian sentiment in Erbil, constructing a public pretext to supply air cover, advanced weaponry, and logistics to separatist militias operating along Iran’s western frontier.\nUltimately, the investigative committee established by Iraqi Prime Minister Ali Faleh al-Zaidi must rigorously examine technical signatures and foreign intelligence footprints rather than relying on surface-level assumptions. Erbil and Tehran share a vital imperative to resist external manipulation, disarm destabilizing armed groups, and ensure foreign covert operations cannot subvert regional sovereignty or compromise neighborly stability.\n \n  ",
