        "title": "Fairphone Gen 6 Plus rocks Murena's /e/OS, and it's making all the right moves in its August launch",
        "link": "https://www.androidcentral.com/phones/fairphone-gen-6-plus-rocks-murenas-e-os-and-its-making-all-the-right-moves-in-its-august-launch",
        "source": "Latest from Android Central",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-19T00:00:28.652669+00:00",
        "image": "https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/QGyB2b6ugt8SNbjcbWu2Bd-1060-80.jpg",
        "full_content": "Fairphone Gen 6 Plus rocks Murena's /e/OS, and it's making all the right moves in its August launch\nSustainable and privacy-conscious.\nWhat you need to know\n- Fairphone and Murena have teamed up to debut the Gen 6 Plus with /e/OS, a privacy-focused software based on Android.\n- The Gen 6 Plus delivers 12GB of RAM, 12 replaceable parts for consumers, and a five-year warranty/five years of software updates.\n- Murena Backup debuts with the Fairphone Gen 6 Plus, integrated into Murena Workspace Accounts, alongside the Advanced Privacy widget.\n- The Fairphone Gen 6 Plus is available for $699 in a new Cobalt Blue colorway.\nIf Fairphone's Gen 6 caught your eye last year, the company's latest Gen 6 Plus is taking sustainability even further.\nTogether with Murena's /e/OS, Fairphone launches the Gen 6 Plus, categorizing it as its \"latest achievement in the mission to make technology fairer, more modular, repairable and long-lasting while prioritising user privacy and experience.\" The original Fairphone Gen 6 launched in June 2025, but the company says the Plus model isn't anything to overlook.\nThe company states the Gen 6 Plus builds on \"what already works\" with the previous device. Fairphone is looking to \"fight back\" against current economic pressures, while improving the phone's lifespan. Repairability is a major highlight for Fairphone, and that's continuing with 12 replaceable parts in the Gen 6 Plus. Additionally, consumers will receive a five-year warranty and five years of software updates, carrying the Gen 6 Plus into 2033.\nElsewhere, Fairphone states the Gen 6 Plus comes equipped with 12GB of RAM and Qualcomm's Snapdragon 7s Gen 4. This is a mid-range chip; however, Qualcomm boosted the SoC with stronger, \"flagship-level\" gaming capabilities. The CPU has been boosted by ~7% over the 7s Gen 3, which the Fairphone Gen 6 debuted with.\nPrivacy-focused software\nMurena stands tall with its privacy-focused software, and the Fairphone Gen 6 Plus will benefit from the latest updates. Murena states its source code is \"fully open.\" This means that anyone can verify that it \"does not collect user data\" in the ways Google collects data. It states Google's OS (Android) has \"tracking embedded in its source code and native apps that are constantly ‘pinging information to Google - with ambiguity surrounding how that data is used and where it ends up.\"\nMurena does away with this. Moreover, /e/OS now has an Advanced Privacy widget. This will let users control the data collected by third-party apps installed on their devices. The Fairphone Gen 6 Plus announcement calls back to Murena's /e/OS 4 update, which rolled out in June. The patch focused on making it easy to switch from Big Tech. Users will find \"one-click\" migrations from Google that transfer their files, dates, emails, contacts, and more to Murena's systems.\nOne feature that was teased in June was cloud backups. That's not debuting with the Gen 6 Plus as \"Murena Backup.\" It states this is \"a new cloud-based backup and recovery solution fully integrated with Murena Workspace accounts.\"\nGet the latest news from Android Central, your trusted companion in the world of Android\nConsumers can purchase the Fairphone Gen 6 Plus from Murena for $699. Fairphone highlights a new colorway: Cobalt Blue. However, you'll also find Forest Green and Horizon Black.\nNickolas is always excited about tech and getting his hands on it. Writing for him can vary from delivering the latest tech story to scribbling in his journal. When Nickolas isn't hitting a story, he's often grinding away at a game or chilling with a book in his hand.\nYou must confirm your public display name before commenting\nPlease logout and then login again, you will then be prompted to enter your display name.",
        "content": "Fairphone Gen 6 Plus rocks Murena's /e/OS, and it's making all the right moves in its August launch\nSustainable and privacy-conscious.\nWhat you need to know\n- Fairphone and Murena have teamed up to debut the Gen 6 Plus with /e/OS, a privacy-focused software based on Android.\n- The Gen 6 Plus delivers 12GB of RAM, 12 replaceable parts for consumers, and a five-year warranty/five years of software u...",
