        "full_content": "Women Not Included: Drugs and clinical trials\nIn a world not designed for women, medicine shaped by male bodies leaves women facing higher risks from everyday drugs.\nAfter working exclusively with male mice while looking for a treatment for type 1 diabetes, Dr Ella Hubber begins to uncover a much bigger issue: modern medicine is not built equally for everyone. Along with journalist Chhavi Sachdev, she explores how decades of clinical research have overlooked women with serious consequences.\nThrough expert interviews, they examine how women were historically excluded from clinical trials, why biological differences matter in how drugs work, and how this has led to higher rates of side effects. The story reveals how gaps in research continue to shape women’s healthcare today.\nAs awareness grows, they also ask what change can look like. More representative trials, pharmaceutical companies held accountable, and medicine finally built for everyone.\nPresenter/Producer: Ella Hubber\nResearcher: Elliott Prince\nEditor: Ilan Goodman\nLast on\nMore episodes\nPrevious\nFeatured\n- \n    .\nBroadcasts\n- Mon 10 Aug 2026 19:32GMTBBC World Service\n- Last Tuesday 04:32GMTBBC World Service Australasia, Americas and the Caribbean, South Asia & East Asia only\n- Last Tuesday 12:32GMTBBC World Service Australasia, East and Southern Africa, News Internet & West and Central Africa only\n- Monday 00:32GMTBBC World Service & Live News\nThe Curious Cases of Rutherford and Fry\nPodcast\n- \n                                        DiscoveryExplorations in the world of science.",
