        "full_content": "Crew Review: High-Yield Checking With Built-In Budgeting for Families\nSome products in this article are from our partners. Read our Advertiser Discloser.\nManaging money as a household is harder than it looks. Most people use a regular checking account at a big bank, then juggle a separate budgeting app, maybe a savings account somewhere else, and possibly a kids’ debit card on top of that. It’s a lot to keep track of.\nCrew is a fintech app that tries to put all of that in one place. It combines a high-yield checking account, built-in budgeting tools, and family banking features – all inside a single app. The goal is to help you organize your money, automate your budget, and earn more interest without switching between apps.\nIn this Crew review, we cover what it is, how it works, who it’s best for, the key features, pricing, and what real users are saying. If you’re looking for a smarter checking account that does more, this review gives you the full picture.\nOverall Rating\nSummary\nCrew is a fintech app that tries to put all of that in one place. It combines a high-yield checking account, built-in budgeting tools, and family banking features\n- \n\t\t\t\t\tAPY on Checking 5\n- \n\t\t\t\t\tLow Fees 5\n- \n\t\t\t\t\tAccessibility 4.5\nPros\n• High-yield checking \n• Debit cards available for kids\n• Unlimited budgeting pockets\n• Cash deposits and mobile check deposit\n• No monthly fees or minimum balances\nCons\n• App-only banking with no desktop login\n• No physical check writing\nTable of Contents\nWhat Is Crew?\nCrew is a financial technology (fintech) company based in Lehi, Utah. It was founded by Gentry Davies and Steve Domino, who previously worked at Divvy, a business expense platform acquired by Bill.com. The app launched publicly and has been growing steadily since 2023.\nCrew is not a bank. Banking services are provided by Bangor Savings Bank, which is FDIC-insured. Your deposits are held at Bangor Savings Bank, so they are protected up to federal insurance limits – $250,000 for individual accounts and $500,000 for joint accounts.\nThe app is available on both iOS and Android. A web app is currently in beta.\nKey highlights at a glance:\n- 2.95% APY on all balances in your checking account (variable rate, no minimum balance required)\n- Unlimited “pockets” to organize your money inside one account\n- Autopilot rules to automate paycheck splits, transfers, and budget top-ups\n- Debit cards for every family member, including kids\n- Joint accounts for couples and families\n- No monthly fees and no minimum balance\n- FDIC insured through Bangor Savings Bank\n- Mastercard debit card accepted anywhere Mastercard is used\n- Raised $3.8 million in seed funding in November 2025\nWho Is Crew For?\nCrew works well for a wide range of people, but it’s especially useful if you fall into one of these groups:\n- Families who want one app for both adult and child banking\n- Parents looking to give kids real debit cards with parental controls\n- Couples managing shared finances through a joint account\n- People who want a high-yield checking account with no minimum balance\n- Anyone who dislikes budgeting apps that require manual input and data imports\n- Users are tired of earning close to zero interest at a traditional bank\n- People who want to automate their budget without a lot of manual work\nCrew may not be the right fit for:\n- People who prefer in-person banking at a physical branch\n- Those who primarily use credit cards and want rewards for spending\n- Anyone who needs to make frequent cash deposits\n- Businesses – Crew is designed for personal and family finances only\nCrew Features\n1. High-Yield Checking Account\nCrew offers a checking account that earns 2.95% APY on your full balance. This rate applies to every dollar you hold in the account – there’s no minimum deposit requirement and no tiered rate structure.\nWhy it matters: Most big bank checking accounts pay close to 0.01% APY. Earning nearly 3% on your everyday checking balance can add meaningful interest over time, especially for families keeping a few thousand dollars in their account at any given time.\nWhat to keep in mind:\n- The APY is variable, meaning it can change over time based on interest rate conditions\n- Crew has adjusted its rate before – the rate was higher (around 3.7%) earlier in 2025 and has since come down to 2.95%\n- The rate is still competitive compared to many online savings accounts\n2. Money Pockets\nPockets are virtual “buckets” inside your single Crew checking account. You can create as many as you need – for example, one for bills, one for savings, one for a vacation fund, one for groceries.\nWhy it matters: You don’t need a separate savings account or multiple bank accounts. Pockets let you visually and mentally divide your money without moving it to another institution. You can also lock a pocket in “piggy bank mode” to avoid dipping into it.\nWhat to keep in mind:\n- All pockets exist within one checking account; they are not separate accounts\n- Some users may prefer true separate accounts for psychological separation\n- You spend from your pockets using one debit card; you simply toggle which pocket the card draws from before making a purchase\n3. Autopilot – Budget Automation\nCrew’s Autopilot feature lets you create rules that move money automatically based on triggers. Triggers can be events like a paycheck arriving or a balance dropping below a set level, or they can be time-based, like every Friday or the 1st of the month.\nWhy it matters: Automation removes the discipline requirement from budgeting. You set your rules once, and Crew handles the rest. For example, you can tell Crew to automatically send 10% of every paycheck to your giving pocket, $500 to bills, and keep the rest in checking — without touching the app every payday.\nWhat to keep in mind:\n- Setting up automation rules requires some initial time and planning\n- Triggers include: paycheck arrival, balance changes, and scheduled dates (weekly or monthly)\n- Actions include: transfer money between pockets, send notifications, or trigger a webhook\n- Webhook support makes Crew unusually flexible compared to most consumer banking apps\n4. Family and Child Accounts\nCrew supports joint accounts for couples and child accounts for kids. Each child gets their own Crew account with a debit card that has their name on it. Kids can log into the app with their own login to check their balance and track spending.\nWhy it matters: Most banking apps bolt on a kid’s account as an afterthought. Crew builds family banking into the core experience. Parents get real-time spending notifications, spend controls, and the ability to set automated allowances.\nWhat to keep in mind:\n- Child accounts are real bank accounts, not just prepaid cards\n- Kids’ accounts earn the same 2.95% APY as adult accounts\n- Teens can receive direct deposit into their Crew account\n- Parents control visibility and spending limits\n- You’ll need to manage your family’s finances in the same app, which works well for some families but may feel like a constraint for others\n5. Automated Allowances\nParents can set up automatic recurring transfers to a child’s account. You define the amount and the schedule, and Crew handles the delivery.\nWhy it matters: Automated allowances teach kids about money while removing the “I forgot to pay your allowance” problem for parents. Kids learn what consistent saving looks like in practice.\nWhat to keep in mind:\n- This feature is useful only if your child already has a Crew account\n- Allowances are tied to Crew pockets, so kids can learn to allocate their money too\n6. Debit Cards and Spending Controls\nEvery account member gets a Mastercard debit card. You can switch which pocket your card draws from at any time inside the app – or update a transaction after the fact if you accidentally spent from the wrong pocket.\nWhy it matters: This setup means budgeting is “baked in” to your spending. Instead of tracking what you spent after the fact, you decide which budget category you’re spending from before or at the time of purchase.\nWhat to keep in mind:\n- Cards work anywhere Mastercard is accepted, including internationally\n- Virtual card support is available; you can create unique card numbers for specific recurring bills, set spending limits, and cancel them without affecting your main card\n- There are no credit cards available through Crew, which means no rewards points or cash back on spending\n7. ATM Access\nYou can use your Crew Mastercard at any ATM in the Mastercard, Maestro, or Cirrus networks. Crew does not have its own fee-free ATM network, but it reimburses ATM fees for up to 20 withdrawals per year.\nWhy it matters: The annual ATM fee reimbursement covers most casual cash users without adding much complexity.\nWhat to keep in mind:\n- If you withdraw cash more than 20 times per year, you’ll pay ATM fees out of pocket beyond that\n- Frequent cash users may prefer a bank with a dedicated fee-free ATM network\n8. Wire Transfers\nCrew supports outgoing wire transfers. The fee depends on your total account balance.\n- Free for accounts with over $50,000 in total deposits\n- $20 fee per outgoing wire if your balance is under $50,000\nIncoming wires and standard ACH transfers are processed as usual through the app.\n9. FDIC Insurance\nDeposits held through Crew are insured through Bangor Savings Bank, a Member FDIC institution.\n- Individual accounts: insured up to $250,000\n- Joint accounts: insured up to $500,000\nThis is standard FDIC pass-through insurance. Crew’s website states that pass-through insurance is subject to certain conditions set forth in the deposit agreement.\n10. AI Financial Assistant (Penny)\nCrew includes an AI-powered financial assistant called Penny. Penny can answer questions about your account, help you set up automations, and give you guidance on your financial situation.\nWhy it matters: Penny gives users a simple way to interact with their finances through natural language, without digging through menus.\nWhat to keep in mind:\n- Penny is still a relatively new feature and is continuing to improve\n- It is not a licensed financial advisor and should not replace professional financial guidance\nCrew Fees and Account Limits\nOne of Crew’s stronger selling points is its simple, low-fee structure. Here’s a clear breakdown:\n| Fee / Feature | Amount / Details | \n| Monthly Fee | None | \n| Minimum Balance | None | \n| Overdraft/NSF Fee | None | \n| Checking APY | 2.95% (variable, no minimum required) | \n| FDIC Insurance (Individual) | Up to $250,000 | \n| FDIC Insurance (Joint) | Up to $500,000 | \n| Outgoing Wire Transfer (under $50k balance) | $20 | \n| Outgoing Wire Transfer (over $50k balance) | Free | \n| ATM Fee Reimbursements | Up to 20 withdrawals per year | \n| International Debit Card Use | Works anywhere Mastercard is accepted; see deposit agreement for exchange rates | \n| Account Setup Time | Under 2 minutes for most applicants | \nNote: APY is variable and may change at any time. The 2.95% rate is the most recent published rate. Always check trycrew.com for the current rate before opening an account.\nHow to Sign Up for Crew\nOpening a Crew account is quick. Most people complete it in under two minutes. Here are the steps:\n- Go to trycrew.com or download the Crew app from the App Store (iOS) or Google Play (Android).\n- Tap “Download Crew” or “Get Started” to begin the application.\n- Enter your legal name, date of birth, physical address, and Social Security number (or other tax ID). This is required for identity verification under federal banking regulations.\n- Review and agree to Crew’s deposit account agreement and terms of use.\n- Fund your account via an ACH transfer from an existing bank account or by setting up direct deposit.\n- Customize your pockets once your account is active. Start with a bill’s pocket and a savings pocket to keep it simple.\n- Set up Autopilot rules to automate your budget if desired.\n- Receive your Mastercard debit card in the mail. You can use virtual cards right away while you wait.\nTo add a family member, go to the Family section of the app and follow the prompts to add a joint owner or create a child account.\nFrequently Asked Questions\nIs Crew a real bank?\nNo. Crew is a financial technology company, not a bank. Banking services are provided by Bangor Savings Bank, Member FDIC, which is a real, federally insured bank. Your deposits are held at Bangor Savings Bank, so they are FDIC insured up to federal limits.\nIs the 2.95% APY a promotional rate?\nThe APY is variable, meaning it can change over time. It is not a limited-time promotional rate in the traditional sense; it applies to your full balance, with no minimum or expiration. However, Crew can adjust the rate when market conditions change. The rate has fluctuated over the app’s history (it was as high as 3.7% in early 2025). Referral sign-ups may qualify for a 0.5% APY boost for the first three months.\nCan I deposit cash into Crew?\nCash deposit support has been in development. Some reviews noted it was not yet available at the time of writing, though the feature has been in the works. It’s worth checking the current app version or Crew’s website for the latest on cash deposits before signing up if this is important to you.\nWhat do I need to open an account?\nYou need your legal name, date of birth, physical address, and a tax ID (typically your Social Security number). Most applicants complete the process in under two minutes.\nHow does Crew make money if there’s no monthly fee?\nCrew earns revenue in two ways: from the interest it earns on deposits held at Bangor Savings Bank, and from merchant fees when you use your Crew debit card to make purchases. This model is common among fintech companies and allows them to offer no-fee accounts while still generating revenue.\nCustomer Reviews and App Ratings\nUser feedback for Crew is largely positive, particularly among families and people who value built-in budgeting features.\nGoogle Play\nRating: 4.8 out of 5 stars (based on 179 reviews as of March 2026)\nPositive trends from Google Play users include:\n- High praise for the pocket system and how easy it makes budgeting\n- Strong ratings for the APY relative to traditional checking accounts\n- Customer service is frequently described as responsive and helpful\n- Families highlight how useful it is to have kids’ banking inside the same app\nCommon critical feedback includes:\n- The web app is still in beta, and some users want a full desktop experience\n- A small number of users initially noted the absence of cash deposit support\n- A few users mentioned wanting a credit card option for earning rewards\nApp Store (iOS)\nCrew’s iOS app carries consistently high ratings. Users describe it as well-designed and easy to navigate. Family features are frequently praised, with parents noting that kids enjoy having their own card and app login.\nGeneral Sentiment\nReviewers across platforms repeatedly mention Crew as a genuine alternative to maintaining separate banking and budgeting apps. The combination of high-yield checking, automatic paycheck splitting, and child accounts in one place is the most-cited reason for switching from other banks or apps.\nThe most consistent piece of constructive feedback is that Crew is still a young product and some features – like the web app – are still catching up to the mobile experience.\nFinal Verdict: Is Crew Worth It?\nCrew is a well-designed fintech product that combines several things that usually require multiple apps or accounts: a high-yield checking account, budgeting through pockets, spending automation, and family banking.\n| Crew is best for: Families who want one app for adult and child banking, people tired of earning near-zero interest at a traditional bank, and users who want to automate their budget without a lot of ongoing manual work. It’s also a solid pick for couples managing money together through a joint account. | \n| Crew may not be the right fit if: You prefer in-person banking, rely heavily on cash deposits, want a credit card with rewards, or need a long track record from a large institution. As a newer, smaller fintech, Crew is still building out features like the web app. | \nOverall, Crew fills a genuine gap. Most checking accounts don’t pay meaningful interest and don’t have built-in budgeting. Crew does both, and it adds family banking on top. For households looking to simplify their financial toolkit and earn more interest on everyday balances, it’s worth a serious look.\nAs always, make sure to read the deposit agreement and check the current APY at trycrew.com before opening an account, since rates are variable and can change.\nThis review is for informational purposes only and does not constitute financial advice. APY rates, fees, and features are subject to change. Always verify current terms directly with Crew at trycrew.com before making any financial decisions.",
