        "full_content": "Marvel’s New ‘Avengers: Doomsday’ Teaser Has Fans Scooping Up This Black Panther Exclusive\nIf you purchase an independently reviewed product or service through a link on our website, Rolling Stone may receive an affiliate commission.\nThe Avengers: Doomsday hype is already making its way to Marvel fans’ shopping carts. This Amazon-exclusive Black Panther collectible is currently a Number One bestseller on the retailer, and it’s available to preorder now. A Doctor Doom collectible tied to the upcoming Marvel movie is also up for preorder, making both characters timely additions for fans counting down to the MCU’s next massive crossover.\nThat’s especially true after Marvel unveiled its latest Avengers: Doomsday special look at D23 (the ultimate Disney fan event). The footage gives fans a closer look at Robert Downey Jr.’s Doctor Doom, who is positioned as the major threat facing heroes from across the Marvel multiverse. Shuri’s Black Panther also appears in the footage, alongside characters from The Avengers, Fantastic Four, and X-Men.\nThe renewed attention on Black Panther comes at an interesting moment for the franchise. On July 25, Marvel announced that David Jonsson will become the next Black Panther in Black Panther 3, taking on the role of T’Challa II. The announcement signals a new chapter for Wakanda, while Letitia Wright’s Shuri remains part of the MCU’s immediate future through Avengers: Doomsday.\nNaturally, Marvel isn’t stopping with Black Panther and Doctor Doom. The latest Doomsday buzz has been accompanied by a growing lineup of Marvel collectibles, including new figures and character merchandise that fans can preorder ahead of the movie.\nDisney Store Daredevil Silver Mask – Limited Edition\nYou don’t have to patrol the streets of Hell’s Kitchen to get your own Daredevil mask. This $79.99 silver replica features an adjustable fit and red-tinted eyes, while the included stand and exclusive lithograph make it easy to display when you’re not wearing it.\nDisney Store Hulk and Spider-Man Minico Figures from Iron Studios\nSpider-Man and the Hulk are teaming up — or at least facing off — in this collectible MiniCo figure set from Iron Studios. The set includes both characters in detailed, stylized poses inspired by Spider-Man: Brand New Day.\nDisney Store Thor Stormbreaker Axe with Light and Sound Effects\nYou may not be worthy of Mjolnir, but you can still get your hands on Thor’s other iconic weapon with this Stormbreaker replica. The Marvel Vault collectible features light and sound effects that bring the MCU-inspired axe to life.\nOf course, there’s plenty more to come. Avengers: Doomsday isn’t scheduled to hit theaters until Dec. 18, 2026, leaving Marvel several more months to reveal new footage, characters, merchandise, and potentially a few surprises we don’t see coming. Until then, the latest collectibles are one way to keep the countdown going. See the most recent D23 Avengers: Doomsday trailer below.",
